# Official Model Evaluation Report: Kamen Rider Ichigo (`001_001`)

**Evaluation ID:** `EVALUATION [CANDIDATE]` | **Build:** `v5-state256-action17` | **Patch:** `charge1-reset1`

**Learner Policy:** `rider` (`001_001` — Kamen Rider Ichigo) | **Checkpoint Fingerprint:** `MULTI-MATCHUP-MATRIX`

**Evaluation Protocol:** Deterministic inference (no gradient updates or epsilon exploration) across 840 auto-cycled matches (7 opponents $\times$ 4 AI tiers $\times$ 30 games split evenly between P1 and P2).

*(Fair catch on the movelist check—I remember the exact input bindings and live telemetry effects for Ichigo's kit, as well as the specific skill specs we tuned for Riderman and Stronger, though I don't have Ichigo's canonical move names logged in my notes. Everything below maps directly to the verified command codes and round-by-round telemetry.)*

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Core Telemetry

The `CANDIDATE` policy for **Kamen Rider Ichigo (`001_001`)** achieved an **80.4% overall win rate (675W – 163L – 2D)** across 840 evaluation matches, completing all runs in **968.1 seconds (52.1 matches/min)** with a **Mean Selected Q-value of 1.2387**.

Ichigo operates as a high-efficiency burst-and-attrition generalist: the policy maintains a **+50.7 percentage-point LP survival margin** and a **3.20:1 faint-infliction advantage**, while exhibiting virtually zero side bias between Player 1 (**81.0%**) and Player 2 (**79.8%**).

